<p>Very nice idea, but the story doesn't so much climax as peter out. Perhaps Joe could realise one morning that he can't remember his dead wife's face anymore - something that makes him doubt his strategy is ever going to work. Or, he's trying to reminisce about a time he talked with his son, but he can't recall anything the boy ever said before the accident.</p>
<p>Small detail, but I'm not sure about using &quot;lorem ipsum&quot; in a formal document to describe word salad. Could use &quot;grammatically valid but meaningless sentences&quot;, &quot;unconnected dialog fragments&quot;, or &quot;nonsensical utterances&quot;.</p>

